<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leucon I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 389–349 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leucon I was ruler of the Bosporan Kingdom from 389 to 349 BCE, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spartocid-dynasty">Spartocid dynasty</a>. He took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feodosia">Theodosia</a> and extended his rule over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindi">Sindi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maeotians">Maeotians</a> east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerch-strait">Kerch Strait</a>, turning a union of Greek cities into a territorial state. He granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> tax-free purchase of grain and was honoured with Athenian citizenship, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demosthenes">Demosthenes</a> records.</p></div>
